diff --git a/src/tools/crawler/README.md b/src/tools/crawler/README.md
index 48949f8..1e95291 100644
--- a/src/tools/crawler/README.md
+++ b/src/tools/crawler/README.md
@@ -47,6 +47,10 @@ Reachable counts (`num_good_nodes`, `node_addrs`, `node_info`, and `all_node_rea
 
 Each qualified `node_info` entry exports the actual handshake `last_verified_at_ms`, actual header proof `chain_verified_at_ms`, pinned `chain_block_hash`, and versioned `chain_proof` marker. A new connection attempt clears prior chain eligibility; unsolicited or repeated headers cannot refresh it. Proofs expire after one hour, and unanswered challenges time out after 30 seconds. A non-answer remains unverified rather than being labeled a different chain. Initial-sync nodes can decline header requests, and pruning does not remove retained headers.
 
+Qualified gossip is exported separately as `gossip_provenance: "zcash-mainnet-qualified-addr-v1"`, `gossip_edges: [{source, target, observed_at_ms}]`, and `gossip_truncated: boolean`. Each directed edge means that the exact source endpoint advertised the target address after completing the pinned header proof in that same session. It is not a confirmed connection between those endpoints, proof that the target serves Zcash, or evidence that the target is reachable. Only actual local receipt time is used; timestamps supplied inside peer advertisements are ignored. Summaries do not refresh receipt timestamps. A fresh empty edge array with `gossip_truncated: false` is a supported observation with no current qualifying advertisements. At most 40,000 edges are exported, selected by newest actual receipt first and stable source/target endpoint ordering for ties; `gossip_truncated: true` explicitly marks omitted qualifying edges without changing any retained evidence timestamp.
+
+Each source retains at most 1,000 targets, matching the maximum addresses accepted in one protocol frame. Repeated targets refresh their actual receipt time; additional new targets beyond the bound are omitted until stored observations expire or the session resets. Receipts expire after ten minutes, and a source must still have a fresh handshake and proof when exported. Starting a new attempt or invalidating its proof clears its advertisements, preventing old gossip from inheriting a newer session's proof. `gossip_edges` and `node_info` use the same cloned source evidence. The legacy `all_*` adjacency fields remain undirected diagnostics with no qualified advertiser provenance and must not be treated as this contract.
+
 This census measures recently observed reachable endpoints with the pinned mainnet history through height 3,520,000. Known shared-history forks that diverged before this checkpoint fail the challenge; future forks sharing it require a reviewed checkpoint update in both crawler and consumers. It does not establish current tip synchronization, honest behavior, unique physical nodes, Tor onion coverage, or complete network coverage. Historical handshake-only snapshots are incompatible with the new census and must not be used as trend baselines.
 
 The following legacy sample illustrates the RPC shape; its values predate chain-proof qualification and are not current measurements:
